# How big is Greenland next to Africa?
subtitle: "Guess Greenland's size next to Africa with a bar, then see why the Mercator map makes the two look the same size."

## How big is Greenland next to Africa?
text: {"font_size":34}
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Africa
      - Greenland
      - DR Congo
      - USA+China+India
    values:
      - 30.37
      - 2.17
      - 2.34
      - 22.72
    icons:
      - {of: globe showing europe-africa, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag greenland, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag congo kinshasa, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag united states, set: twemoji}
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 34
    y_label: Million km²
    bar_colors: each
sources:
    - id: cia
      title: 'The World Factbook: Greenland; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States; China; India'
      authors: CIA
      year: 2025
      finding: Greenland 2,166,086 km²; DR Congo 2,344,858 km²; USA 9.83, China 9.6, India 3.29 million km² (22.7 together)
    - id: afr
      title: Africa
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2025
      finding: Africa covers about 30.4 million km²

    text times "14 ×" #b5482e cites ["afr","cia"] x 450 y 560 font_size 80 hidden true
    icon map size 230 set twemoji x 780 y 520 icon_look picture of "world map" hidden true
    text merc "Mercator, 1569" #2f6b8f x 780 y 385 font_size 40 hidden true
    text fits "room to spare" #2f6b8f x 620 y 620 font_size 40 hidden true

    card title "How big is Greenland next to Africa?"

On most wall maps, Greenland looks about as big as Africa.
    draw axes bar_1

    ask "Africa is drawn. How big is Greenland? Drag its bar to your guess." on bar_2 store g default "20"
        right: Close: you said {g} million square kilometres, and it is {g.true}.
        wrong: You said {g} million square kilometres; it is only {g.true}.

Africa is about fourteen times bigger: thirty million square kilometres against two.
    draw times

The culprit is the map itself, drawn by Gerardus Mercator in 1569 for sailors.
    draw map merc

It keeps compass directions true, so a straight line on it is a steady course across the sea.
    point at.ref bar_2 gesture underline

But to do that it stretches the land more and more toward the poles, and Greenland sits far in the north.
    highlight bar_2 effect circle

In fact Greenland is smaller than a single African country, the Democratic Republic of the Congo.
    draw bar_3

    erase times map merc

And Africa could swallow the United States, China and India together, with room to spare.
    draw bar_4 fits

So next time you see a world map, look twice at the top and bottom.
    highlight bar_1

